    win: 'Alone, you are chasing your own best score. With others, everyone flies at once and the highest score wins.',
    levels: [['Morning class', 'Only stacks of books get in the way.'], ['Fans on', 'Ceiling fans join the books.'], ['Swinging bangles', 'Some bangles swing from side to side. Aim where the bangle will be.'], ['Paper storm', 'The evening light comes in, paper flies through the air, and some books drift across too.'], ['Night class (level 5 and up)', 'The tube lights are on, and the fans bob up and down as well.'], ['Golden bangle', 'Every new level opens with a big golden bangle in the middle: 10 points and full lift.']],
    tips: ['Watch the aim ring, not the chit: when it is green, hold still.', 'Line up the next bangle early: small, steady movements beat big swerves.', 'A combo is worth more than a single safe bangle, but not more than your lift.', 'Watch for a fan just behind a bangle and plan your way out before you go in.'],
    faq: [['Does Flying Chit ever end?', 'No. The bangles get smaller and the room faster, so there is always a better score to chase.'], ['Can I unlock different paper chits?', 'Yes. Earn coins through play, then open Game Styles to unlock a Blueprint Glider, Golden Origami, Neon Comet or Rose Kite. These change the 3D look, not the flight physics.'], ['Can two people play on one screen?', 'Yes. Choose Single Phone: one player uses W A S D and the other the arrow keys, or each uses a gamepad.'], ['Is it like other flying games?', 'It is our own idea: you steer freely in 3D and keep the chit up by flying through bangles, instead of tapping to flap.']],
